title: Aegis APPROVE model switch, with M1 (permit mis-attribution after timeout+reconcile) and M2 (context guard bypass on resume)
summary: |-
  Model picker plus in-process switch (branch worktree-agent-a1ec45f09003354bd; full gnomon 2503 green).
  Verified:
  - human-only at the dispatcher and kernel;
  - law-7 re-run plus a new subscription permit per switch;
  - a concurrent-switch latch;
  - send blocked while switching;
  - strict model validation, the argv token passed separately, no echo;
  - reconcile writes only `to` or `from`, never the observed string.
  M1: after a timeout followed by reconcile-to-new, the session runs the new model on the old model's permit, so per-model tracking is wrong and the confirm text ("budget keeps counting by model") is untrue. Fix: hold the fresh permit through the uncertainty and swap it on reconcile.
  M2: the context guard reads 0 on a resumed session and only guards [1m] sources. Fix: compare against the target's window regardless of source, and refuse while usage is unknown.
  L1: gate on a trusted click, not a form submit. L2: dead-session timeout rows. L3: sanitise Claude's error text. L4: log a failed release.
  Fix builder launched.
symbols_touched:
  - '#session-runner'
  - '#claude-adapter'
  - '#gui-model-picker'
  - $model-switch
learnings:
  - When a fallback path releases a resource and a later reconcile adopts the outcome, the resource must be held until reconcile, or accounting drifts.
  - Guards keyed on the source model miss sources whose defaults change; guard on the target's capacity.
